1. Definitions

   "Licence Key" means a Tares licence key issued by the Licensor. It names an organisation, a
   number of Seats and an expiry date.

   "Seat" means one person listed on a Tares instance.

   "Production" means any use other than development and testing. Use by people for their real
   work is Production.

2. Running Tares without a Licence Key

   The Software ships inside Tares. You may install and run Tares with the Software present and
   no Licence Key. Without a Licence Key its enterprise features stay off and Tares runs for one
   person.

3. Development and testing

   You may copy and modify the Software for development and testing. Modified copies stay under
   this licence.

4. Production use

   You may use the enterprise features of the Software, including your own modifications, in
   Production only with a valid Licence Key issued to your organisation, for your organisation's
   own use, and for no more Seats than that Licence Key allows. Contractors working for you count
   as Seats. You may not share or transfer a Licence Key.

5. Expiry

   Your right to Production use under section 4 ends on the expiry date of your Licence Key
   unless you renew it. Tares may keep working after that date so that a lapsed key does not
   interrupt your work. That does not extend this licence.

6. Distribution

   You may distribute unmodified copies of the Software only as part of a distribution of Tares
   that includes this licence, such as a fork, mirror, package or container image. You may share
   modified copies only for development and testing, and under this licence.

   You may not otherwise copy, sublicense or sell the Software, or any part of it. You may not
   offer the enterprise features of the Software to third parties as a hosted or managed service.

7. Licence checks and notices

   You may not use the Software in Production with a licence key check removed, changed or
   bypassed. This includes a check in the MIT-licensed part of Tares. You may not remove or change
   the licensing notices in the Software.

